@Chaosus I wonder why are `^`, `~` and `,` treated as invalid characters. The first two are weird to ban.

Regarding caret and tilde, page 14 of the [GLSL ES spec](https://registry.khronos.org/OpenGL/specs/es/3.0/GLSL_ES_Specification_3.00.pdf) (under the preprocessor chapter) lists `^` as a valid bitwise XOR operator and `~` as a valid bitwise negation (invert bits) operator.

Sorry if I don't understand this code at all, does this run only after macro expansion? Is so, it makes sense to ban comma, but if not, it's used to separate macro parameters, both in definitions and in calls.

